The Round-To-Even Function

Comparison of ROUND and ROUNDE (Round-To-Even) Functions
-------------------------------------------------------

x          Round(x)     RoundE(x)   
---------- ----------   ----------  
0          0            0           
0.25       0            0           
0.5        1            0           
0.75       1            1           
1          1            1           
1.25       1            1           
1.5        2            2           
1.75       2            2           
2          2            2           
2.25       2            2           
2.5        3            2           
2.75       3            3           
3          3            3           
3.25       3            3           
3.5        4            4           


Comparison of estimates that use full data and rounded data
PROC MEANS data=Round sum mean ndec=3;
Label Length="True values" Round="Rounded values" RoundEven="Round-to-even values";

Variable                  N          Sum         Mean
-------------------- ------ ------------ ------------
Length (True values)    425      429.530        1.011
Round (Rounded values)    425      432.800        1.018
RoundEven (Round-to-even values)    425      427.900        1.007


Proportion rounded up
PROC MEANS data=Round mean ndec=3;

Variable                                      N         Mean
---------------------------------------- ------ ------------
Proportion rounded up for ROUND             425        0.548
Proportion rounded up for ROUNDE            425        0.433

